<script lang="ts">
	import { englishExamples as examples } from '../../utils/examples.en'

	const comment = signal('')
	const accepted = signal(false)
	const notifications = signal(true)
	const period = signal('week')
	const volume = signal(40)
	const days = signal('30')
	const dayOptions = [
		{ value: '7', label: '7 days' },
		{ value: '30', label: '30 days' },
		{ value: '90', label: '90 days' },
	]
	const range = signal('month')
	const ranges = [
		{ value: 'today', label: 'Today' },
		{ value: 'week', label: 'This week' },
		{ value: 'month', label: 'This month' },
		{ value: 'quarter', label: 'This quarter' },
		{ value: 'year', label: 'This year' },
		{ value: 'all', label: 'All time' },
	]
	const periods = [
		{ value: 'day', label: 'Day' },
		{ value: 'week', label: 'Week' },
		{ value: 'month', label: 'Month' },
		{ value: 'year', label: 'Year', disabled: true },
	]
</script>

<template>
	<DocsPage
		locale="en"
		title="Form controls"
		description="Textarea, Checkbox, RadioGroup, SegmentedControl, Switch and Slider: native HTML, with its keyboard and submission, and the look of UI."
	>
		<p>
			They all keep the native control, so the keyboard, the focus and form submission are those of the browser, also without JavaScript. Their models bind to a signal:
			<code>model="field"</code>.
		</p>
		<h2 id="textarea">UITextarea</h2>
		<p>
			Inside
			<MeekoLink to="/forms">UIField</MeekoLink>
			it receives the id and the description, and the field paints the counter.
		</p>
		<DocsPreview layout="stack">
			<UIField
				id="comment"
				label="Comment"
				hint="Optional"
				bind:counter="comment.value.length + '/200'"
			>
				<snippet
					name="default"
					params="id, describedBy"
				>
					<UITextarea
						name="comment"
						placeholder="What would you like to tell us"
						model="comment"
						bind:rows="4"
						bind:maxlength="200"
						bind:id="id"
						bind:describedBy="describedBy"
					/>
				</snippet>
			</UIField>
		</DocsPreview>
		<DocsCode bind:code="examples.textarea" />
		<DocsApi
			caption="UITextarea props"
			bind:rows="[
				{ name: 'model', type: 'Signal<string>', default: 'Empty string', description: 'Text, two-way.' },
				{ name: 'rows / name / maxlength / placeholder', type: 'HTML attributes', description: 'They reach the textarea as they are.' },
				{ name: 'required / disabled', type: 'boolean', default: 'false', description: 'Native state.' },
				{ name: 'invalid / describedBy', type: 'boolean / string', description: 'aria-invalid and aria-describedby.' },
				{ name: 'class', type: 'string', description: 'Additional classes.' },
			]"
		/>
		<h2 id="checkbox">UICheckbox and UISwitch</h2>
		<p>
			<code>UISwitch</code>
			has the same contract as
			<code>UICheckbox</code>, with <code>role="switch"</code>: use it for something that applies at once.
		</p>
		<DocsPreview layout="stack">
			<UICheckbox
				label="I accept the terms"
				description="You can withdraw it later."
				name="accepted"
				value="yes"
				model="accepted"
			/>
			<UISwitch
				label="Notifications"
				name="notifications"
				model="notifications"
			/>
			<p
				id="controls-status"
				class="docs-status"
				role="status"
			>
				{accepted.value ? 'Terms accepted.' : 'Terms not accepted.'} {notifications.value ? 'Notifications on.' : 'Notifications off.'}
			</p>
		</DocsPreview>
		<DocsCode bind:code="examples.checkbox" />
		<DocsApi
			caption="UICheckbox and UISwitch props"
			bind:rows="[
				{ name: 'model', type: 'Signal<boolean>', default: 'false', description: 'Checked state, two-way.' },
				{ name: 'label', type: 'string', description: 'Required. Visible label.' },
				{ name: 'description', type: 'string', description: 'Supporting text under the label.' },
				{ name: 'name / value', type: 'string', description: 'What the form sends.' },
				{ name: 'required / disabled', type: 'boolean', default: 'false', description: 'Native state.' },
				{ name: 'invalid / describedBy', type: 'boolean / string', description: 'aria-invalid and aria-describedby.' },
				{ name: 'class', type: 'string', description: 'Additional classes.' },
			]"
		/>
		<h2 id="radio">UIRadioGroup</h2>
		<p>
			A
			<code>fieldset</code>
			with its
			<code>legend</code>
			and a native radio per option: the arrows move the selection.
			<code>variant="segmented"</code>
			paints it as a compact switcher.
		</p>
		<DocsPreview layout="stack">
			<UIRadioGroup
				legend="Period"
				name="period"
				model="period"
				bind:options="periods"
			/>
			<UIRadioGroup
				legend="Period, segmented"
				name="period-segmented"
				variant="segmented"
				model="period"
				bind:options="periods"
			/>
		</DocsPreview>
		<DocsCode bind:code="examples.radio" />
		<DocsApi
			caption="UIRadioGroup props"
			bind:rows="[
				{ name: 'model', type: 'Signal<string>', description: 'Chosen value, two-way.' },
				{ name: 'legend', type: 'string', description: 'Required. Name of the group.' },
				{ name: 'options', type: 'readonly UIRadioOption[]', description: 'Required. value, label and disabled.' },
				{ name: 'name / required / disabled', type: 'string / boolean', description: 'Native submission and state.' },
				{ name: 'variant', type: 'default | segmented', default: 'default', description: 'A list of radios or a compact switcher.' },
				{ name: 'class', type: 'string', description: 'Additional classes.' },
			]"
		/>
		<h2 id="segmented">UISegmentedControl</h2>
		<p>
			A compact single choice, such as the period of a chart: the same native radios as
			<code>UIRadioGroup</code>
			with the look of a segmented control, so the arrows, form submission and
			<code>required</code>
			also work without JavaScript. Its total height is the one of a control of its size,
			<code>sm</code>
			or
			<code>md</code>, and it lines up with a
			<code>UIButton</code>
			next to it.
		</p>
		<p>
			It needs a name:
			<code>legend</code>, which
			<code>hideLegend</code>
			leaves to screen readers only, or
			<code>ariaLabel</code>. When the options do not fit, the control scrolls sideways inside its own width: no option breaks and the page does not get wider.
		</p>
		<DocsPreview layout="stack">
			<UISegmentedControl
				legend="Chart period"
				hideLegend
				size="sm"
				name="days"
				model="days"
				bind:options="dayOptions"
			/>
			<p
				id="segmented-status"
				class="docs-status"
				role="status"
			>
				Showing the last {days.value} days.
			</p>
			<UISegmentedControl
				legend="Range"
				name="range"
				model="range"
				bind:options="ranges"
			/>
		</DocsPreview>
		<DocsCode bind:code="examples.segmented" />
		<p>
			<code>UIRadioGroup variant="segmented"</code>
			is still available and wraps into several lines when it does not fit; for a compact switcher, use
			<code>UISegmentedControl</code>. Its
			<code>size</code>
			takes an application value in
			<code>ui.defaults.segmentedControl</code>.
		</p>
		<DocsApi
			caption="UISegmentedControl props"
			bind:rows="[
				{ name: 'model', type: 'Signal<string>', description: 'Chosen value, two-way.' },
				{ name: 'options', type: 'readonly UIRadioOption[]', description: 'Required. value, label and disabled.' },
				{ name: 'legend', type: 'string', description: 'Name of the group, in its legend. Required without ariaLabel.' },
				{ name: 'hideLegend', type: 'boolean', default: 'false', description: 'The legend for screen readers only.' },
				{ name: 'ariaLabel', type: 'string', description: 'Name of the group without a legend, instead of legend.' },
				{ name: 'size', type: 'sm | md', default: 'md', description: 'Height and text, those of a control of that size.' },
				{ name: 'name / required / disabled', type: 'string / boolean', description: 'Native submission and state.' },
				{ name: 'class / ui', type: 'string / object', description: 'Classes of the fieldset and of base, legend, options, option and input.' },
			]"
		/>
		<h2 id="slider">UISlider</h2>
		<p>
			An
			<code>input type="range"</code>
			with the label inside its
			<code>label</code>. The filled part of the track follows the value.
		</p>
		<DocsPreview layout="stack">
			<UISlider
				label="Volume"
				name="volume"
				model="volume"
				bind:min="0"
				bind:max="100"
				bind:step="5"
			/>
			<p
				id="slider-status"
				class="docs-status"
				role="status"
			>
				Volume: {volume.value}
			</p>
		</DocsPreview>
		<DocsCode bind:code="examples.slider" />
		<DocsApi
			caption="UISlider props"
			bind:rows="[
				{ name: 'model', type: 'Signal<number>', default: '50', description: 'Value, two-way.' },
				{ name: 'label', type: 'string', description: 'Required. Visible label.' },
				{ name: 'min / max / step', type: 'number', default: '0 / 100 / 1', description: 'Native limits and step.' },
				{ name: 'name / disabled', type: 'string / boolean', description: 'Native submission and state.' },
				{ name: 'class', type: 'string', description: 'Additional classes.' },
			]"
		/>
		<p>
			The types
			<code>UITextareaProps</code>, <code>UICheckboxProps</code>, <code>UISwitchProps</code>, <code>UIRadioGroupProps</code>,
			<code>UISegmentedControlProps</code>
			and
			<code>UISliderProps</code>
			are exported from
			<code>@meekojs/ui/runtime</code>.
		</p>
	</DocsPage>
</template>
